# Pairs with BackupSagaConsistent (the requested SweepReadsLiveUnderGate). A
# self-terminalise or retroactive sweep reads the coordinator's live verdict
# under the gate instead of a local decision, and applies a terminal for a
# txid this tree has not decided, breaking invariant I1: that shard reads
# post-saga while another still resolves the saga against the snapshot.
MODULE: BackupSagaConsistentSweepReadsLiveUnderGate
TARGET: BackupSagaConsistent
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a sweep applies a terminal from a live coordinator verdict while the gate is held
PERTURBS: Sweep

--- FIND
Sweep(t, sh) ==
    /\ sh \in Writes(t)
    /\ prep[t][sh]
    /\ term[t][sh] = "none"
    /\ loc[t][TreeOf[sh]] # "none"
    /\ term' = [term EXCEPT ![t][sh] = IF loc[t][TreeOf[sh]] = "committed" THEN "commit" ELSE "abort"]
--- REPLACE
Sweep(t, sh) ==
    /\ sh \in Writes(t)
    /\ prep[t][sh]
    /\ term[t][sh] = "none"
    \* MUTATION: under the gate the read dials the coordinator.
    /\ \/ loc[t][TreeOf[sh]] # "none"
       \/ Gated(TreeOf[sh]) /\ dec[t] # "inflight"
    /\ LET v == IF loc[t][TreeOf[sh]] # "none" THEN loc[t][TreeOf[sh]] ELSE dec[t]
       IN term' = [term EXCEPT ![t][sh] = IF v = "committed" THEN "commit" ELSE "abort"]
--- END
